      "round_summary": "Repair round 2 (re-fix): Fixed assertion_error in usb_phy.scala (line 96-100). Root cause: assertStableWhen fires on the transition cycle where rst_cnt goes 30→31 and io.usb_rst goes 0→1 simultaneously. Fix: replaced assertStableWhen with fvAssert using RegNext-based temporal sampling. RegNext(usb_rst_cond, false.B) and RegNext(rst_cnt, 0.U) snapshot the condition and counter value from the previous cycle. The assertion checks stability only when usb_rst_cond was true in BOTH the current AND previous cycle — correctly skipping the transition cycle. Original assertion label 'rst_cnt_stable_during_usb_rst' preserved. Inspected source: assertStableWhen used only once, no homologous assertions. Using RegNext instead of past() API because past() returns Unit (statement form) not a value-returning expression in ChiselFv.",
